  "description": "B-grade Sean Connery sci-fi\nflick or a place beyond the closet. It's my personal belief that Outland\nis short for \"Outlandishly affordable Shimano 9-speed equipped mountain\nbike.\" And it is.\n\nAll that shifting happens by way of Shimano Deore 9-speed shifters and\nderailleurs that swoop you from the itty bitty 11-tooth high gear to the\nroot-pulling 32-tooth low in single, double or triple clicks. So you can\nplink from one gear to it's neighbor to fine-tune your pedal speed to\nmatch your comfort level, or wail your way across a bunch of cogs when\nthat sweet downhill you're on suddenly dips into the inevitable uphill\nthat follows.\n\nBut don't forget to stop all that gear clicking and tune into how sweet\nit is to feel your leg power translated into motion by the Outland's Custom\n7005 alloy frame with PowerDiamond down tube, TrailTuned custom tapered\nstays and Edge S-bend MonoStay. You'll also appreciate the bump-smoothing\nprowess of SunTour's XCP-D suspension fork with 80mm of spring-cushioned\nvertical compliance.\n\nWant more stopping power within your budget? Feel free to swap out your\nlinear-pull stoppers for a pair of Avid's Mechanical Discs because the\nOutland comes to you disc ready. Lucky you.",
